---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import LegalDocument from "../components/LegalDocument.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of Service — Filosign"
	description="Terms of Service for Filosign document signing software and optional on-chain USDC payout automation."
>
	<div
		class="min-h-screen bg-background font-manrope selection:bg-primary/10 selection:text-primary"
	>
		<Navbar />
		<main>
			<LegalDocument
				title="Terms of Service"
				description="These terms describe how Filosign provides document signing software and optional on-chain payment automation. They are not legal advice."
				lastUpdated="May 2026"
			>
				<h2>1. Service</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign provides software for sending, signing, and verifying
					documents. Optional features may include USDC payout rules executed via
					public smart contracts on supported networks.
				</p>

				<h2>2. Non-custodial payments</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign does not hold, pool, or transmit your USDC. Payouts use a
					pull-payment model: you register rules and approve the settlement validator
					from your own wallet; settlement is <code>transferFrom</code> from your
					wallet to the recipient when release conditions on the document registry
					are met.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						You control <code>registerRule</code> and token <code>approve</code>
						transactions from your wallet.
					</li>
					<li>
						Filosign does not sign payout transactions on your behalf.
					</li>
					<li>
						You may revoke funding by setting token approval to zero (e.g.
						<code>approve(validator, 0)</code>) before a payout executes.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>3. Supported product path vs direct contract use</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>Supported path:</strong> creating payments through the Filosign
					app or API when sending a document. On that path, Filosign enforces
					product rules (for example, payout recipients limited to envelope
					participants or your organization&apos;s linked payout wallet) and may
					index payment status for the UI and compliance exports.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Direct contract use:</strong> you may interact with deployed
					contracts without the app. Filosign does not apply product policies to
					those transactions and does not guarantee that status, indexing, or
					automation covers rules created outside the supported path.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong
						>Filosign does not control or screen, and hence is not responsible
						for, all on-chain payouts.</strong
					>
					Execution of <code>executePayout</code> is permissionless when contract
					conditions are met: any address (including Filosign server relay or your
					wallet) may submit the transaction. Paying gas does not bypass signature
					requirements enforced by the contracts.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Automation and indexing</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Filosign may automatically relay <code>executePayout</code> from its
						server when conditions are met (server-paid gas). You may also submit
						settlement yourself from the sign page when offered.
					</li>
					<li>
						Database and in-app payment status generally reflect rules submitted
						through <code>files.register</code> after on-chain verification.
						On-chain rules created only outside Filosign may still execute on-chain
						but may not appear in the app.
					</li>
					<li>
						Filosign does not guarantee that a payout will execute (for example,
						insufficient balance, revoked approval, or unmet release conditions).
					</li>
					<li>
						If a payout is executed outside Filosign (without using Settle payment
						or Settle from wallet on the sign page), in-app status and compliance
						indexing may update within approximately one day via a daily on-chain
						scan. Funds still transfer on-chain regardless of dashboard timing.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>5. Compliance screening</h2>
				<p>
					When wallet screening is enabled, it applies to the Filosign send and
					registration path—not to every <code>registerRule</code> call on the
					blockchain by wallets that do not use Filosign.
				</p>

				<h2>6. Assumption of risk</h2>
				<p>
					Smart contracts, wallets, and blockchain networks involve technical
					risk (bugs, chain reorganizations, failed transactions). You are
					responsible for reviewing amounts, recipients, and approvals before you
					sign transactions.
				</p>

				<p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground pt-6">
					Contact: <a href="https://x.com/filosign" class="underline"
						>@filosign</a
					>. See also our <a href="/privacy" class="underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
				</p>
			</LegalDocument>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
